Thought: To identify the SMILES string of the organic compound, I should first gather some spectral data to understand its structure. The most informative and cost-effective initial step would be to obtain the molecular formula, which can be derived from the mass spectrometry spectra. This will help narrow down the possibilities for the SMILES string.
Action: mass_spectrometry_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: The mass spectrometry data provides the most intense peak at m/z 235.1395, which likely corresponds to the molecular ion peak. This suggests a molecular weight of approximately 235.14 g/mol. To proceed, I should determine the molecular formula that matches this molecular weight. Once I have the molecular formula, I can explore possible isomers and their SMILES strings.
Action: obtain_isomers_from_molecular_formula
Action Input: {"molecular_formula": "C15H17NO2"}

Thought: I have obtained a list of possible isomers for the molecular formula C15H17NO2. To identify the correct SMILES string, I should compare these isomers against the NMR data of the compound. I will start by obtaining the proton NMR spectra to see which isomer matches the observed chemical shifts.
Action: proton_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}
